  "era": "Aqua gloss to iOS 6 leather shutdown",
  "summary": "Stitched leather, felt card tables and glossy buttons — software as furniture.",
  "description": "Skeuomorphism is interface design imitating physical material: Apple's iOS Game Center felt tables, Notes app legal pads with tear-off holes, Calendar's leather stitching, Find My Friends' tanned hide, and Aqua's candy-gloss buttons before it. The era (2001-2013, peaking with iOS 4-6) argued that metaphor teaches — your phone as a desk of familiar objects — and produced the richest (and most ridiculed) ornament in software history: rendered shadows, glass reflections, velvet gradients. Jony Ive's iOS 7 (2013) flattened the world overnight, and skeuomorphism is now period style: quoted in \"neo-skeuomorph\" games, watch-face craft, and every design-history lecture about the metaphor debate.",
  "culturalContext": "Skeuomorphism is design's great metaphor debate: Apple's leather and felt taught interfaces through physical metaphor, iOS 7's flattening ended the era overnight, and the look is now period style — quoted in neo-skeuomorph games and every design-history lecture about ornament's return.",
